  introText: A quiet evening at home. It is still light outside, so look around your apartment while you can.
  outageText: The power just went out and the sun is setting! Night 1 begins. Check the fuse box. Watch your water and food, or you won't survive.
  newDayText: Day {0} begins. The sun is up. Use the daylight to prepare for the next night.
  dayTips:
  - Keep a stock of drinking water. Plan on about 2 liters per person per day.
  - 'Eat perishable food first: without cooling it is only safe for about 4 hours.'
  - A battery-powered or hand-crank radio keeps you informed when mobile networks and internet fail.
  - Never use grills, camping stoves or generators indoors. Carbon monoxide is invisible and deadly.
  - Check on elderly or sick neighbors. They may need help or medication.
  - Use flashlights instead of candles. Candles are a fire risk, especially when unattended.
  - Keep some cash at home. Card readers and cash machines may not work during an outage.
